          'content': 'THE 8 DIRECTIONS:\n\n              NORTH (N)\n                 |\nNORTH-WEST  ---[+]--- NORTH-EAST\n(NW)             |            (NE)\nWEST --------[CENTER]-------- EAST\n(W)              |            (E)\nSOUTH-WEST  ---[+]--- SOUTH-EAST\n(SW)             |            (SE)\n              SOUTH (S)\n\nTURN RULES:\nFacing North:\n→ Turn LEFT = Face West\n→ Turn RIGHT = Face East\n→ Turn BACK (180°) = Face South\n\nFacing East:\n→ Turn LEFT = Face North\n→ Turn RIGHT = Face South\n→ Turn BACK = Face West\n\nFacing South:\n→ Turn LEFT = Face East\n→ Turn RIGHT = Face West\n→ Turn BACK = Face North\n\nFacing West:\n→ Turn LEFT = Face South\n→ Turn RIGHT = Face North\n→ Turn BACK = Face East\n\nMEMORY TRICK FOR TURNS:\nLeft turns go ANTICLOCKWISE: N→W→S→E→N\nRight turns go CLOCKWISE: N→E→S→W→N\n\nDISTANCE CALCULATION:\n\nCase 1 — Straight line (same direction)\nTotal distance = sum of all movements in same direction minus opposite movements\n\nCase 2 — Perpendicular movements (L-shaped path)\nUse Pythagoras: Distance = √(horizontal² + vertical²)\n\nCommon Pythagorean triplets to memorize:\n3-4-5: √(9+16) = 5\n5-12-13: √(25+144) = 13\n6-8-10: √(36+64) = 10\n8-15-17: √(64+225) = 17\n7-24-25: √(49+576) = 25\n\nEXAMPLE PROBLEM:\nRavi starts from A, walks 6km North, turns right and walks 8km East. What is the shortest distance from starting point?\nSolution: Horizontal = 8km, Vertical = 6km\nDistance = √(6²+8²) = √(36+64) = √100 = 10km\n\nDIRECTION AFTER TURNS PROBLEM:\nStarting facing North:\n- Turn right 90° → Now facing East\n- Turn right 90° → Now facing South\n- Turn left 90° → Now facing East\n\nSHADOW PROBLEMS:\nMorning (sun rises in East) → Shadow falls WEST\nEvening (sun sets in West) → Shadow falls EAST\nNoon → Shadow falls NORTH (in India/tropical regions)\n\nEXAM TIPS:\n• ALWAYS draw a diagram — never try mentally\n• Mark North direction first, then trace the path\n• For shadow problems: morning=West shadow, evening=East shadow\n• Time: 45-60 seconds per question',
