          'content': 'LINES AND ANGLES:\n• Complementary angles: sum = 90°\n• Supplementary angles: sum = 180°\n• Vertically opposite angles: always equal\n• Linear pair: two angles on a straight line = 180°\n\nPARALLEL LINES (cut by transversal):\n• Corresponding angles: equal (F-shape)\n• Alternate interior angles: equal (Z-shape)\n• Co-interior angles: supplementary = 180° (C-shape)\n\nTRIANGLES — PROPERTIES:\n• Sum of all angles = 180°\n• Exterior angle = sum of two non-adjacent interior angles\n• Sum of any two sides > third side\n• Greater angle has greater opposite side\n• Pythagoras: In right triangle, hypotenuse² = base² + height²\n\nPythagorean Triplets (memorize all):\n3-4-5, 5-12-13, 8-15-17, 7-24-25\n6-8-10 (= 2× 3-4-5), 9-12-15 (= 3× 3-4-5)\n10-24-26 (= 2× 5-12-13)\n\nTRIANGLE AREA FORMULAS:\n• Basic: Area = ½ × base × height\n• Heron\'s formula: Area = √[s(s-a)(s-b)(s-c)] where s=(a+b+c)/2\n• Equilateral triangle: Area = (√3/4)a², Height = (√3/2)a\n• Right triangle: Area = ½ × product of two perpendicular sides\n\nCENTRES OF TRIANGLE:\n• Centroid (G): Intersection of medians. Divides median in 2:1\n• Circumcentre (O): Centre of circumscribed circle\n• Incentre (I): Centre of inscribed circle (equidistant from all sides)\n• Orthocentre (H): Intersection of altitudes\n\nCIRCLE:\n• Area = πr² (≈ 22/7 × r² or 3.14r²)\n• Circumference = 2πr\n• Diameter = 2r\n• Area of sector = (θ/360°) × πr²\n• Arc length = (θ/360°) × 2πr\n• Area of segment = Area of sector - Area of triangle\n\nChord properties:\n• Perpendicular from centre to chord bisects the chord\n• Equal chords are equidistant from centre\n• Tangent to circle is perpendicular to radius at point of contact\n• Tangent-chord angle = inscribed angle in alternate segment\n\n2D SHAPES:\nRectangle: Area = l×b, Perimeter = 2(l+b), Diagonal = √(l²+b²)\nSquare: Area = a², Perimeter = 4a, Diagonal = a√2\nParallelogram: Area = base × height\nRhombus: Area = (d1×d2)/2, Perimeter = 4a\nTrapezium: Area = ½(sum of parallel sides) × height\n\n3D SHAPES:\nCuboid: V = l×b×h, TSA = 2(lb+bh+lh), Diagonal = √(l²+b²+h²)\nCube: V = a³, TSA = 6a², Diagonal = a√3\nCylinder: V = πr²h, CSA = 2πrh, TSA = 2πr(r+h)\nCone: V = (1/3)πr²h, l = √(r²+h²), CSA = πrl, TSA = πr(r+l)\nSphere: V = (4/3)πr³, SA = 4πr²\nHemisphere: V = (2/3)πr³, CSA = 2πr², TSA = 3πr²\n\nIMPORTANT RELATIONSHIPS:\n• Cone volume = (1/3) × Cylinder volume (same r and h)\n• Sphere volume = Cylinder volume when 2r=h... No: Sphere=(4/3)πr³\n• Largest sphere in cube: radius = side/2\n• Largest circle in square: radius = side/2',
